findings.mechanism:
lookupDraw calls validateVariant without the `live` output, so masked=false and any differing captured dword is a miss. Draw variants are built without dataPositions or flatBinding. Per-object constants that the shader reads through the SRT end up in the captured runs; when they change each frame, every stage that reads them misses. The miss then:
- recaptures and rematerializes (a new snapshot means a result-memo miss);
- deep-copies the result;
- inserts a variant (maximum 4 per stage), evicting older ones.
Dispatch handles the same case with EqualData: it patches the FlattenedSrt binding words into a copy of the cached result.
